{
  "name": "image-approval-pipeline",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Image approval pipeline (starter)\n\nApprove a prompt once, then render on ComfyUI, downscale, and prove review-serve reachability.\n\nPorts the retired workflow-runner spec (branch eb198d5) to n8n built-in nodes only.\n\n**Runtime variables** live in the `Runtime variables` (Edit Fields) node: comfy_server, review_server, max_height, project, artifact_id, variant_prompt. Change them there, everything downstream reads them by expression.\n\nProven-working vs stubbed: see workflows/README.md.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky-overview",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -360,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### ComfyUI poll loop\n`Render done?` false branch loops back to `Poll wait 2s`.\nMinimal by design (no max-tries cap yet).\nTODO: add an iteration counter + timeout to fail loudly instead of looping forever.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "sticky-loop",
      "name": "Poll loop",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        820,
        480
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Downscale is a wired STUB\n`Downscale (PIL)` is **disabled** (passes input through).\nStock n8n image has no python3/Pillow, so `scripts/n8n-container/downscale.py` cannot run in-container as-is.\nEnable after mounting the script + providing python3+Pillow, OR run downscale on the host.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "sticky-downscale",
      "name": "Downscale gap",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1900,
        420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Publish = reachability probe only\nreview-serve has NO HTTP publish endpoint; `push` is CLI-only.\n`Publish reachability probe` GETs `/_/api/settings` to prove 2xx connectivity.\nReal publish needs a new HTTP push endpoint on review-serve (follow-up) or an Execute Command node with review-serve.py + staging dir mounted in.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "sticky-publish",
      "name": "Publish gap",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2240,
        420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### A/B compare (optional, disabled)\nMirrors the retired `ab_compare`: it COMPOSES comfy_render + publish for a second prompt.\nThese nodes are duplicated-but-labeled copies (kept in one importable file rather than a sub-workflow for starter clarity).\nEnable + wire seeds to compare variant_prompt against the approved prompt.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 360,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky-ab",
      "name": "A/B compare",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2620,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "formTitle": "Approve render prompt",
        "formDescription": "Approve the prompt as-is, or edit it before rendering. This is the only interactive step.",
        "formFields": {
          "values": [
            {
              "fieldLabel": "prompt",
              "fieldType": "textarea",
              "placeholder": "a red fox sitting in snow, photograph, golden hour",
              "requiredField": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "responseMode": "lastNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "approve",
      "name": "Approve prompt",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.formTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        300
      ],
      "webhookId": "approve-prompt-webhook"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "v1",
              "name": "comfy_server",
              "value": "http://host.containers.internal:8188",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "v2",
              "name": "review_server",
              "value": "http://host.containers.internal:9099",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "v3",
              "name": "max_height",
              "value": 1080,
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "id": "v4",
              "name": "project",
              "value": "image-approval",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "v5",
              "name": "artifact_id",
              "value": "image-approval-latest",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "v6",
              "name": "variant_prompt",
              "value": "a red fox in snow, oil painting, dramatic light",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "v7",
              "name": "approved_prompt",
              "value": "={{ $json.prompt }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "includeOtherFields": false,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "vars",
      "name": "Runtime variables",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        240,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Build the ComfyUI API-format graph from the approved prompt + a fresh seed.\n// Template mirrors spikes/comfyui-driver/workflow.json. Node ids match the\n// retired steps.py: COMFY_PROMPT_NODE=\"6\" (CLIPTextEncode positive),\n// COMFY_SEED_NODE=\"3\" (KSampler). A fresh seed every call avoids a silent\n// ComfyUI cache hit (identical graph -> empty outputs = failure).\nconst approvedPrompt = $('Runtime variables').first().json.approved_prompt;\nconst seed = Math.floor(Math.random() * 2147483647);\n\nconst graph = {\n  \"4\": { \"class_type\": \"CheckpointLoaderSimple\", \"inputs\": { \"ckpt_name\": \"sd_xl_base_1.0.safetensors\" } },\n  \"5\": { \"class_type\": \"EmptyLatentImage\", \"inputs\": { \"width\": 1024, \"height\": 1024, \"batch_size\": 1 } },\n  \"6\": { \"class_type\": \"CLIPTextEncode\", \"inputs\": { \"text\": approvedPrompt, \"clip\": [\"4\", 1] } },\n  \"7\": { \"class_type\": \"CLIPTextEncode\", \"inputs\": { \"text\": \"blurry, low quality, watermark\", \"clip\": [\"4\", 1] } },\n  \"3\": { \"class_type\": \"KSampler\", \"inputs\": { \"seed\": seed, \"steps\": 12, \"cfg\": 7, \"sampler_name\": \"euler\", \"scheduler\": \"normal\", \"denoise\": 1, \"model\": [\"4\", 0], \"positive\": [\"6\", 0], \"negative\": [\"7\", 0], \"latent_image\": [\"5\", 0] } },\n  \"8\": { \"class_type\": \"VAEDecode\", \"inputs\": { \"samples\": [\"3\", 0], \"vae\": [\"4\", 2] } },\n  \"9\": { \"class_type\": \"SaveImage\", \"inputs\": { \"filename_prefix\": \"image-approval\", \"images\": [\"8\", 0] } }\n};\n\nreturn [{ json: { prompt: graph } }];\n",
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems"
      },
      "id": "buildgraph",
      "name": "Build ComfyUI graph",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        480,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $('Runtime variables').first().json.comfy_server }}/prompt",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "submit",
      "name": "Submit render",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        720,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "amount": 2,
        "unit": "seconds"
      },
      "id": "wait",
      "name": "Poll wait 2s",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.wait",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        960,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "={{ $('Runtime variables').first().json.comfy_server }}/history/{{ $('Submit render').first().json.prompt_id }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "pollhist",
      "name": "Poll history",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        1200,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "leftValue": "={{ Object.values($json)[0] ? Object.keys(Object.values($json)[0].outputs || {}).length : 0 }}",
              "rightValue": 0,
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "gt"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "done",
      "name": "Render done?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        1440,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Pull the first rendered image's filename/subfolder/type out of ComfyUI's\n// /history response so the next node can GET /view for it.\nconst history = $json;\nconst entry = Object.values(history)[0] || {};\nconst outputs = entry.outputs || {};\nfor (const out of Object.values(outputs)) {\n  for (const img of (out.images || [])) {\n    return [{ json: { filename: img.filename, subfolder: img.subfolder, type: img.type } }];\n  }\n}\nthrow new Error('no image in ComfyUI history output (cache hit or still rendering)');\n",
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems"
      },
      "id": "extract",
      "name": "Extract image ref",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1680,
        200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "={{ $('Runtime variables').first().json.comfy_server }}/view",
        "sendQuery": true,
        "specifyQuery": "keypair",
        "queryParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "filename",
              "value": "={{ $json.filename }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "subfolder",
              "value": "={{ $json.subfolder }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "type",
              "value": "={{ $json.type }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "responseFormat": "file"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "fetch",
      "name": "Fetch image",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        1920,
        200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "command": "=python3 /data/scripts/downscale.py --src /data/render.png --max-height {{ $('Runtime variables').first().json.max_height }} --out /data/preview.png"
      },
      "id": "downscale",
      "name": "Downscale (PIL)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeCommand",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2160,
        200
      ],
      "disabled": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "={{ $('Runtime variables').first().json.review_server }}/_/api/settings",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "publish",
      "name": "Publish reachability probe",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        2400,
        200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "r1",
              "name": "review_url",
              "value": "={{ $('Runtime variables').first().json.review_server }}/_/review?artifact={{ $('Runtime variables').first().json.artifact_id }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "includeOtherFields": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "reviewurl",
      "name": "Compose review URL",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        2640,
        200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Build the ComfyUI API-format graph from the approved prompt + a fresh seed.\n// Template mirrors spikes/comfyui-driver/workflow.json. Node ids match the\n// retired steps.py: COMFY_PROMPT_NODE=\"6\" (CLIPTextEncode positive),\n// COMFY_SEED_NODE=\"3\" (KSampler). A fresh seed every call avoids a silent\n// ComfyUI cache hit (identical graph -> empty outputs = failure).\nconst approvedPrompt = $('Runtime variables').first().json.variant_prompt;\nconst seed = Math.floor(Math.random() * 2147483647);\n\nconst graph = {\n  \"4\": { \"class_type\": \"CheckpointLoaderSimple\", \"inputs\": { \"ckpt_name\": \"sd_xl_base_1.0.safetensors\" } },\n  \"5\": { \"class_type\": \"EmptyLatentImage\", \"inputs\": { \"width\": 1024, \"height\": 1024, \"batch_size\": 1 } },\n  \"6\": { \"class_type\": \"CLIPTextEncode\", \"inputs\": { \"text\": approvedPrompt, \"clip\": [\"4\", 1] } },\n  \"7\": { \"class_type\": \"CLIPTextEncode\", \"inputs\": { \"text\": \"blurry, low quality, watermark\", \"clip\": [\"4\", 1] } },\n  \"3\": { \"class_type\": \"KSampler\", \"inputs\": { \"seed\": seed, \"steps\": 12, \"cfg\": 7, \"sampler_name\": \"euler\", \"scheduler\": \"normal\", \"denoise\": 1, \"model\": [\"4\", 0], \"positive\": [\"6\", 0], \"negative\": [\"7\", 0], \"latent_image\": [\"5\", 0] } },\n  \"8\": { \"class_type\": \"VAEDecode\", \"inputs\": { \"samples\": [\"3\", 0], \"vae\": [\"4\", 2] } },\n  \"9\": { \"class_type\": \"SaveImage\", \"inputs\": { \"filename_prefix\": \"image-approval\", \"images\": [\"8\", 0] } }\n};\n\nreturn [{ json: { prompt: graph } }];\n",
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems"
      },
      "id": "abbuild",
      "name": "Build variant graph (B)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        2880,
        200
      ],
      "disabled": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $('Runtime variables').first().json.comfy_server }}/prompt",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "absubmit",
      "name": "Submit variant render",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        3120,
        200
      ],
      "disabled": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "={{ $('Runtime variables').first().json.review_server }}/_/api/settings",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "abpublish",
      "name": "A/B publish probe",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        3360,
        200
      ],
      "disabled": true
    }
  ],
